--- G9: footing independence ---------------------------------------------
  In the deep regime the pinning and the K-matter density both scale as v_flat^2,
  so their RATIO and mu_K^match have the closed footing-free form
      mu_K^match(r) = 1/(r sqrt(ln(R_max/r)))
  Graded at fixed radius r (kpc) on the deep rows only (x >= 10 on BOTH footings):
  the small-x rows are footing-dependent through ln(R_max/r) with R_max fixed in kpc
  -- a convention, disclosed, not a physical footing effect.
  worst relative difference canonical vs alt on the deep rows: 2.876e-03 at (10.45, 100.0, 'mu_K_match', 15.436285645447025, 16.969444298499706)
  G9: FAIL as frozen (line 1e-6)
  DIAGNOSIS (not an amendment): the residual is the finite-x correction to the
  asymptotic closed form, and it falls with x.  Per row (log M_b 10.45):
    r  100.0 kpc  x_can   15.44  x_alt   16.97  mu_K^match   6.8052 /   6.7857  residual 2.876e-03
    r  272.0 kpc  x_can   41.99  x_alt   46.16  mu_K^match   3.2605 /   3.2571  residual 1.069e-03
    r  389.0 kpc  x_can   60.05  x_alt   66.01  mu_K^match   2.6677 /   2.6657  residual 7.490e-04
    r  637.0 kpc  x_can   98.33  x_alt  108.10  mu_K^match   2.3496 /   2.3485  residual 4.582e-04
  The ASYMPTOTIC statement (mu_K^match = 1/(r sqrt(ln(R_max/r))), no a0, no M_b,
  no kernel) is exact; what is footing-dependent is the finite-x correction to it.
  G9 is not load-bearing: §5's labels are set by G1-G5 and G7 / G8 / G10.

