--- G11: kappa -----------------------------------------------------------
  a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lam),  rho_Lam = Omega_L rho_crit, Omega_L = 0.685, H0 = 67.4
    kappa(canonical) = 0.4999   (by construction from that footing's a0)
    kappa(alt      ) = 0.6041   (by construction from that footing's a0)
  measured, from the record's fits: 0.551 +/- 0.043 (distance-free), 0.465 +/- 0.076 (BTFR)
  DERIVED by this carrier?  NO -- and the reason is exact (G2/H4 above):
    in the deep regime rho_c = (a0/g) rho_b + partial_s g/(4 pi G);
    outside the baryons that is partial_s g/(4 pi G), which contains no a0.
    Under a0 -> lam a0 with g fixed the halo density is INVARIANT, so no
    observable of this carrier fixes kappa.  kappa is a FLAT DIRECTION here.

